cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "WYDCurvature: a Lean 4 proof of the Gibilisco–Isola conjecture on the scalar curvature of the Wigner–Yanase–Dyson metrics"
authors:
  - family-names: Bornemann
    given-names: Adam
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
license: Apache-2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24548331
repository-code: "https://github.com/Charmooo/WYDCurvature"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A formal proof, in Lean 4 with Mathlib, of Conjecture 8.1 of P. Gibilisco and
  T. Isola (J. Math. Phys. 46 (2005), arXiv:math-ph/0407007): the scalar
  curvature of the Wigner–Yanase–Dyson metric WYD(p) on the faithful density
  matrices is Schur-increasing, that is, monotone under mixing, for p near 1.
  It is proved for every p ≤ −1 and every p ≥ 1/2 and every matrix size, strictly
  for p ≠ 2, where the curvature is constant; the case p = 1 is the Kubo–Mori
  metric and Petz's conjecture, brought in from PetzCurvature. The statements use
  the paper's own definitions. With β = 1/p, WYD(p) is the pullback of a constant
  pairing by ρ ↦ (ρ^β, ρ^(1−β)), which gives a closed form of the scalar curvature
  through the Gauss equation and reduces the conjecture to Dittmann's four
  inequalities for an explicit kernel. Two of them are proved by hand, one through
  an autonomous ODE system and a barrier argument; the other two through Newton
  expansions of exponential polynomials whose coefficients are polynomials with
  nonnegative integer coefficients, checked in the kernel. Also proved is
  Theorem 6.1 of the same paper: the function f_p of the WYD(p) metric is
  normalized symmetric operator monotone exactly for p ≤ −1 and p ≥ 1/2, through
  an operator geometric mean, in any unital C*-algebra for the "if" direction.
